    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A mortal thrall who served the Tremere for nearly five centuries before finally being Embraced by Karl Schrekt in 1882, Maxwell Ldescu now rules Berlin's Tremere as its de facto Primogen, granted authority over any clanmate who comes to the city. He personally maintains the Chantry in West Berlin and keeps carefully concealed havens on both sides of the divided city. Deeply opposed to the chaos of anarchy, he has quietly worked to stop the Final Reich's more violent demonstrations before they can break the Masquerade &mdash; a project complicated by the fact that the Reich's true master is his own estranged childe, Heinrich Himmler, secretly a Sabbat agent. Both princes court his favor, aware his vote may ultimately decide who rules a reunified Berlin. He dreams of becoming prince himself one day.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Easygoing and friendly until someone noses into your affairs. When angered, go cold and quiet, letting your target know they are close to death.</p>",
    "notes": "Haven: the Chantry, West Berlin, plus concealed havens on both sides of the city. Sire of Heinrich Himmler, unaware his childe secretly serves the Sabbat. Both princes treat him warily and court his favor.",
